        "d6db2712-5a18-444e-bf6a-fb414cbaa869": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "",
            "subheading": "",
            "text": "<p>Many people think that hair loss only affects men. However, it is estimated that <strong>more than 50% of women will experience noticeable hair loss. <\/strong>Forty percent of <em>women<\/em> have visible <em>hair loss<\/em> by the time they are age 40, according to the American Academy of Dermatology<\/p><p><strong>Hair loss in women can be absolutely devastating for self image and emotional well-being.<\/strong> <\/p><p><strong>Thinning hair can grow back depending on what caused it to thin in the first place<\/strong>. Individuals who experience thinning hair due to<br\/>nutrient deficiencies, stress, pregnancy, and other non-genetic reasons could<br\/>experience regrowth.<\/p>",
            "width": "50%",
            "alignment": "center",
            "align_text": "left",
            "text_size": "medium",
